<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mosbach</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mosbach is a town on the edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odenwald">Odenwald</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neckar">Neckar</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, known for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a>-framed old town. From 1410 to 1499 it was the seat of the Palatinate-Mosbach line of the Wittelsbachs, after which it returned to the Electoral Palatinate. It passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> in 1806.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mosbach.jpg" alt="Mosbach" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AlterVista · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mosbach_Merianblick_3.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
